most superhero games give you all the  power you are of course the hero of the  story with marvel's guardians of the  galaxy idos montreal is taking a  different approach putting you into a  superhero team with the focus on making  you feel like part of the group you  can't handle everything on your own but  it's remarkable how through the teamwork  mechanics within the game you quickly  start to feel like you can work together  with the other guardians to stop any  obstacle we recently got a chance to  play a chapter of guardians of the  galaxy which showed off some of how  you'll interact with the other members  of the team as the story unfolds and how  you'll act as the guardian's leader on  the battlefield if you want to see more  guardians coverage from gamespot make  sure to hit the like and subscribe  buttons below  the portion we played takes place on a  nova core station called the rock where  the guardians had to pay a fine in order  to get the interstellar fuzz off their  backs it starts in typical guardians  fashion the team doesn't agree on the  best course of action gamora thinks it's  a good idea to settle up on the fine  even though it's costly so the guardians  won't have to keep looking over their  shoulders rocket on the other hand wants  to just make a run for it and keep the  cash as peter quill aka star-lord you  agree with gamora even before you take  off though you have the opportunity to  talk to the other members of the squad  that includes a quick heart to heart  with rocket to convince him that his  opinion is valued among the guardians  and a chance to learn about gamora's  secret hobby collecting dolls soon after  landing at the rock the guardians  quickly start to suspect that something  is wrong none of the space bureaucrats  are at their posts and the station  appears to be empty so there's no one to  pay the fine to the group decides to  head further into the station but to do  that you need rocket to put his  engineering skills to work to help open  some doors that highlights the guardian  request system when you need someone  else on the team to do something you can  ask them for help but they may not  always just follow orders in this case  you need rocket to get the doors open  but he's not thrilled about having to  crawl through ducts and mess with wires  there's also a puzzle that needs solving  and using quill's special visor you can  have a look around the room to complete  the circuit connections that power the  door you can also power up a vending  machine to help drax grab a drink and  you can accidentally power up a  defective console that blows up almost  in gamora's face causing her to yell at  you for your carelessness all of those  little moments are optional but they  each trigger more dialogue among the  guardians that continues to develop  their characters and adds more humor to  the goings-on later when you hit another  locked door that requires rocket's  expertise he straight up refuses to open  it which demonstrates why idos is  calling it the guardian request system  rocket is tired of wandering around the  station looking for people and unless  quill agrees that he's not going to lead  them through the entire rock rocket  won't open any more doors for the group  with the request system you can also try  to ask the other guardians for  assistance since they don't have the  expertise they instead will weigh in on  the situation leading to some fun jokes  like drax suggesting you negotiate with  the rodent rocket eventually agrees to  open the door but only after quill  agrees to end the search after just one  more room that one room of course is the  turning point of the level when you find  a nova corps helmet and are able to  listen into local communications here  you start to get a sense of what's going  on when you hear some weird religious  chatter between the nova troopers and  apparently they're searching for someone  this also presents one of the major  choice moments in the level where you  can decide to either speak up and ask  the nova corps folks what's going on or  remain silent on our first playthrough  in the chapter we stayed silent and  through the next door we found an  elevator with a glass wall through it  the guardians watched as some novacore  soldiers with weird purple halos of  energy around their heads executed some  of their comrades seems like some kind  of cultish mind control situation is  happening and since we didn't make our  presence known on the radio the  guardians were able to sneak into the  room and take the cultists by surprise  that kicked off combat for the first  time where we got a sense of how  teamwork permeates all levels of the  game quill on his own isn't a  particularly strong fighter he carries a  couple of guns and sports his signature  jet boots allowing you to run or fly  around the battlefield to hit different  targets or drop into cover but while  quill's guns do some damage and he can  fight hand to hand neither is always  super effective against all enemies  luckily quill's guns have elemental  add-ons that give you different benefits  in the demo we had access to an ice  element that allowed quill to freeze  enemies which made them easy targets for  the other guardians in combat the rest  of your team will take on enemies on  their own with each fighting in their  own way rocket sports an arsenal of  heavy weapons groot ties enemies up with  his roots and drax and gamora close the  distance to fight with melee weapons or  hand to hand but you can still use the  guardian request system here where you  can call on each member of the team to  use specific abilities on individual  targets so freezing a tough enemy with  quills guns allows you to then call on  drax to hit that enemy with a big attack  doing massive damage gamora's assassin  abilities are great for taking out  distant snipers while groot can tie up  multiple enemies with his vines and  briefly take them out of the battle  rocket has a powerful grenade that's  great for damaging several enemies at  once  so alone none of the guardians are  particularly strong or suited for every  situation but together they're extremely  formidable  as quill it's up to you to give orders  in the fight paying attention to what  threats are the priority and knowing  which guardians can best deal with them  the demo quickly started mixing tougher  enemies with the grunts as we fought our  way through them including a big guy who  sported an energy shield that made him  tough to shoot using groot or drax to  distract that enemy was key allowing  quill to flank him to avoid the shield  blasts from the freeze gun left the  enemy vulnerable so gamora could get in  and do some big damage and if you  attacked the enemy in the back you could  destroy the shield generator taking away  its defensive advantage if the guardians  are hurt or caught in a trap like the  electric mines the shield enemy would  sometimes send out it was up to quill to  help them or break them free leave the  guardians on their own too long and they  start to go down like squad mates in  games such as gears of war requiring you  to revive them if you're winning the  fight and playing effectively though the  game rewards you with a sort of combo  tracker that shows just how well you're  synergizing with the guardians and that  boosts your experience point gains  eventually you can initiate a momentary  boost called the huddle which also  charges on a timer the huddle pauses the  action and brings the guardians to quill  for a quick pep talk but you have to  make sure you're paying attention to  your squad in order to effectively pump  them up the different members of your  team will talk about how the fight is  going using keywords that hang on your  screen you then have two options for  your response and you need to pick the  pep talk response that's right for the  situation if the guardians are  demoralized you can reiterate that the  group is capable of taking on anything  when they work together if they're  fighting over who's kicking more ass you  can implore them not to get cocky and to  support each other so everyone can kick  even more ass the huddle is a great  emergency measure because it  automatically revives anyone on the team  who is downed even if you pick the wrong  answer but if you pick the right one the  guardians are energized by quills  coaching and everyone gets a momentary  damage boost when they get back into the  fight it's another way the game  emphasizes the team over the individual  and reiterates that you're a key part of  the group playing through the demo a  second time also showed how choices can  impact combat encounters if you choose  to talk to the novacore through the  helmet a group of cultists will come  looking for you and you lose the element  of surprise when they show up forcing  you into a fight in the next scene when  you're in the elevator the cultist  enemies know you're coming and they open  fire on the glass window so instead of  getting the drop on enemies drax  literally leaps out of the elevator and  starts wailing on people quill's jet  boots allow him to follow but the rest  of the team can't just jump down three  stories so the first part of the fight  is just quill and drax while you wait  for the other guardians to catch up and  in order to make it through you really  have to step up for your game as a  leader a few moments later the rest of  the team joins the battle and their  banter reflects how you did you might  hear rocket remark that the team owes  drax a beer for ripping through the  enemy novacore if you do well in the  fight so ultimately your choices might  lead to the same places it seems but not  necessarily in the same way  while your decisions with the guardians  and how you treat them might influence  how the story unfolds and their  relationships with you idos montreal  noted that they won't affect combat  rocket might complain about opening a  door because you haven't been listening  to him throughout a mission but that  doesn't mean he's going to refuse orders  while you're in combat ido said it  didn't want players to feel panelized by  their choices in combat so the team will  always fight to their fullest when it  counts but in between battles the  interpersonal dynamics come through and  the guardians pay attention to your  choices like whether you risked speaking  on the nova corps radio or stayed quiet  we also got a sense of how progression  will work in guardians of the galaxy  throughout the level you can find  supplies on the ground to collect  specifically two different kinds of  materials gathering those materials  allows you to upgrade quills gear at  work benches unlocking new abilities for  yourself like boosts for your boots or  upgrades for your guns and your scanner  that can give you information about  enemies fighting well also earns you  experience points you can spend on any  of the guardians to unlock new abilities  you can add to quill's arsenal of moves  like adding the ability to hover over  the battlefield to get better sight  lines on enemies or throw more options  to the rest of the guardians for when  you use the request system in a fight  each of the moves has different stats so  you can see how much each attack will  damage enemies how many people it can  target how long it will make your  cooldown timer last and how much it  contributes to filling up enemies  stagger meters which can stun them and  leave them open to more attacks knowing  what abilities are good in which  situations is essential to winning  fights and the better job you do  synergizing each team member's moves the  more experience you earn to buy new  abilities the demo ended soon after a  few more big fights with various enemies  requiring changes and tactics in order  to deal with each one the team finally  made their way back to their ship with  the guardians constantly bantering and  joking the whole way through through  combat character moments between fights  and the decision points throughout the  demo it was remarkable how much  guardians of the galaxy captures the  feeling of being a member of a team even  if the rest of the team is controlled by  ai it all suggests that guardians of the  galaxy is a superhero game that's not  going to feel like other superhero games  but it does a great job of capturing the  humor dysfunction and camaraderie that  makes the guardians of the galaxy such a  great group of characters  chew move over  what are you looking at  oh no you ain't chewing through any more  of my ship my ship  shoot [ __ ] off
 

